{"summary":"Equinix Q2 2026 (ended June 30 2026) reported total revenue of **$2.625 billion**, up 16% year‑over‑year, with **$2.377 billion of recurring revenue (90.6%)** and **$248 million non‑recurring (9.4%)**. Management stated that “the vast majority” of its largest Q2 deals were AI‑workload driven. The company closed **134 MW of xScale leases** in Q2, including the Hampton transaction that generated roughly **$120 million of non‑recurring fees**, about **4.6% of total Q2 revenue**. No disclosed percentage of total leasing or revenue is attributed specifically to AI.

On the macro side, Fed policy in 2025–26 was a valuation and financing variable for data‑center REITs, but AI/cloud leasing demand and backlog conversion increasingly outweighed rate sensitivity. The 2025 sector posted a –14.2% total return despite 21.3% FFO growth; by mid‑2026 data‑center REITs returned +33.2% with 29.4% FFO growth. A 50‑bp cap‑rate rise from 4.4% to 4.9% reduces NOI‑by‑cap‑rate value by ~10.2% holding NOI constant; the implied 2025 data‑center REIT cap rate was about 4.4%.

Sources: S1.4, S2.1, S6.1‑S6.3 (Equinix Q2 2026 results and AI leasing); S8.1‑S8.6, S8.16 (data‑center REIT rate sensitivity and sector performance)."}
